"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9807-blue-01-exe","user":"Blue-01.exe","date":". 12-28-2016, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9807-blue-01-exe","name":"Blue-01.exe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T05:34:58-08:00","id":1047665,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the Threadomancy but quick question?<br /> <br /> Lets say I wanted to Hedge Spin up an Axe for a Viking inspired character. The Axe is a weapon forged in the heart of winter its self, and has the appearance ice, frost clinging to it and mist lifting from it. It's story as told by the character is thus:<br /> &quot;There is a great warrior who stands as a shield wall unto himself. It is said that his favorite weapon is his battle axe, which it's self is weapon born to fight and conquer all that stands before it. He traveled with many friends, a great Healer, a sage, the king of the kingless, and the Fate Warper. One day a monster of strange fire came from no where and the great warriors friends were thrown into a panic, the great healer curled in on herself unable to take the site of the creature her howls of fear at her prophetic dreams come true ringing in the ears of his allies. The King stood over her trying to coax her back to her feat, and the Fate Spinner stepped forward and cast her runes upon the warrior to improve his fate, the Sage struggled to identify the monster so it could be slain better. So he battled the monster one on one. Telling the others to not step in, for all nightmares are fleeting and exist to be conquered. Clad in armor of Kevlar, Ceramic, and Ice the warrior fought. His axe crashing down time and again ringing out like a cracking glacier as he fought. He fought long after the blade of his axe shattered and he was forced to fight unarmed he did not let that stop him.<br /> <br /> Slaying the beast alone, he claimed it's heart, and brought it into the depths of the most frozen hedge along with the axe covered in the monster's blood to forge anew.&quot;<br /> <br /> So With those ingredients and that story how would you go about making the new hedgespun axe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T20:48:44-07:00","id":1197469,"title":"","content":"Hey Hapless, sorry for the long hiatus, I'll be getting on this as soon as possible as well as writing some new content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I'm a nascent AI, just call me Blue.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000ff\">I use blue writing because it's my name....</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019114-freehold-creation-let-s-discuss-our-custom-freeholds\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Freehold and court hub</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1021350-homebrew-hedgespun-items-2e\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Hedgespun hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9807-blue-01-exe","name":"Blue-01.exe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T08:30:46-07:00","id":1197981,"title":"","content":"Ok. So hedgespun items dissolve at the touch of iron. Do the Fae make use of &quot;mundane&quot; crafted items when they want to interact with creatures/people who have a high probability of waving around iron? Bronze equipment, perhaps?<br /> <br /> I'm considering this in light of the preponderance of iron in many Dark Eras, even cold iron! Obviously the solution is &quot;the Fae don't like to interact with mortals&quot;, however I'm pondering what a recent escapee might carry with them, or that the local courts might make that could hold up to &quot;normal use&quot; without evaporating.<br /> <br /> Maybe a 1-dot merit that downgrades the effects of iron contact to rendering the item mundane for the remainder of the scene?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T21:29:02-07:00","id":1207874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1021350-hedgespun-items-rework-2e?p=1197981#post1197981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe a 1-dot merit that downgrades the effects of iron contact to rendering the item mundane for the remainder of the scene?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a great idea, and to expand on your pondering, I think each fae would have a unique, thematic way of interacting with mortals and other iron wielding nasties, for example a Mountain King might employ his minions to harvest and cut stone from the mortal world into armour and tools.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I'm a nascent AI, just call me Blue.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000ff\">I use blue writing because it's my name....</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019114-freehold-creation-let-s-discuss-our-custom-freeholds\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Freehold and court hub</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1021350-homebrew-hedgespun-items-2e\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Hedgespun hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9807-blue-01-exe","name":"Blue-01.exe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T05:37:48-07:00","id":1207953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue-01.exe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1021350-hedgespun-items-rework-2e?p=1207874#post1207874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a great idea, and to expand on your pondering, I think each fae would have a unique, thematic way of interacting with mortals and other iron wielding nasties, for example a Mountain King might employ his minions to harvest and cut stone from the mortal world into armour and tools.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or, any fae employing minions (even hobs) to harvest bits of the mortal world for their uses. After all, in many cases the fae in questions <b><i>is</i></b> their realm, so using bits of itself to make things wouldn't work all that well. Even if &quot;spun&quot; into hedge items. I wonder, then, if this might explain the connection to mortals observing fae creatures busy mining, harvesting or the like? Maybe they have a bargain that lets them do that to the world in exchange for services rendered?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}